config MPIPE_VID
	bool "Video plugin support"
	select VIDEO
	help
	  Elements backed by Zephyr video devices: capture from a camera, and
	  memory-to-memory transforms performed by hardware such as a scaler,
	  rotator or decoder.

	  This is where zero-copy matters most, so the pools here hand out the
	  driver's own buffers rather than copies, and a frame captured by a
	  camera reaches the display without being moved.

if MPIPE_VID

config MPIPE_VID_CONVERT
	bool "Software-based pixel format converter"
	help
	  A transform that converts a frame from one pixel format to another on
	  the CPU.

	  It exists as the fallback for a conversion no hardware on the board can
	  do, which is common between a decoder's output format and what a panel
	  accepts. It converts pixel formats only: it does not scale, crop or
	  rotate. Expect it to cost real CPU time per frame.

config MPIPE_VID_OVERLAY
	bool "Rectangle overlay"
	help
	  An in-place transform drawing rectangle outlines into the frames
	  passing through, typically detection boxes from an inference
	  running beside the pipeline. The application updates the set of
	  rectangles at any time through a property.

config MPIPE_VID_OVERLAY_MAX_RECTS
	int "Rectangles the overlay holds"
	depends on MPIPE_VID_OVERLAY
	range 1 255
	default 16
	help
	  Upper bound on the rectangles drawn into one frame. The element
	  keeps a copy of the set, and copies it again on the stack for each
	  frame, so this sizes both.

endif # MPIPE_VID
